$ocr — optical character recognition (PaddleOCR)

SUMMARY
  Runs PaddleOCR on each images[] file and writes recognized text into texts[]
  (one .txt per image).

SYNTAX
  $ocr
  $ocr(lang='en')
  $ocr(lang='es')
  $ocr(lang='ru', gpu=True)

INPUT
  images[] — source images (PNG, JPG, …)

OUTPUT
  texts[] — one text file per image (lines = detected text regions)

ARGUMENTS
  lang=    — language code (default en). Top packs:
              en English, zh/ch Chinese, hi Hindi, es Spanish, fr French,
              ar Arabic, pt Portuguese, ru Russian, ja Japanese, de German,
              id Indonesian, vi Vietnamese, tr Turkish, it Italian, ko Korean,
              uk Ukrainian, pl Polish, nl Dutch, ur Urdu, fa Persian
  gpu=     — use GPU when true (default CPU; or AH_OCR_GPU=1)
  no_cls=  — disable angle classifier when true

MODELS
  Shared packs under models/ocr/PP-OCRv4/{pack}/ (en, ch, latin, arabic, …).
  Latin pack covers es/fr/de/pt/it/id/vi/tr/pl/nl. Cyrillic covers ru/uk.
  Arabic pack covers ar/ur/fa. Devanagari covers hi.
  First run downloads automatically.

DEPENDENCIES
  uv sync --extra ocr   (paddlepaddle 3.2.x — avoid 3.3+ on CPU)

ENVIRONMENT
  AH_EMULATE_OCR=1 — placeholder text, no Paddle load.
  AH_OCR_GPU=1     — default gpu=True when arg omitted.
  CPU inference disables OneDNN and Paddle IR fusion (Windows/Paddle 3.x compat).

EXAMPLE
  @scan: $file('receipt.png') -> $ocr(lang='es')

PROMPT-CONSUMING
  No — images[] pass through; input texts[] are replaced.
